==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Dogenstein]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Prof. Owlbrowley]] spawns after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Mr. Mer]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Prof. Owlbrowley]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 73.33 seconds<sup>2,200f</sup>.
**1 [[Tarsiriel]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**1 [[Angelic Sleipnir]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
**1 [[Mr. Mer]] spawns after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage can be extremely difficult due to the heavy support Mr. Mer is given. Because of this, it is recommended you bring [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]], such as [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], to block the constant [[Mini-Wave]]s from Mr. Mer. You can also bring [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attacker]] such as [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] or [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]] to deal with Prof. Owlbrowley and Tarsiriel due to their decently slow attack rates, allowing you to time your Jelly Dumpling Cats to deal damage from afar. [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] works amazingly here, dealing huge damage to Mr. Mer, chipping Owlbrowley and Sleipnir while also having Wave Immunity. Due to the surplus of cash, you do not need to worry about him draining your money.

You can use meatshields such as [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] or [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]] to help deal with Angelic Sleipnir—the latter being [[Immune to Knockback]]—since he is only buffed to 250% and can be easily killed with the right units (e.g. [[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kalisa]], [[Ushiwakamaru (Legend Rare Cat)|Colossal Benkei]] and Supernova Cosmo, or alternatively a stack of well-protected [[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cats]]).

